# Same trap as build/modules/mod-dk-lowlevel/.gitignore, for the same reason: the repo-root
# .gitignore line 12 is a bare `data/`, which -- having no leading slash -- matches a directory
# named `data` at ANY depth. It is there for the extracted client data at the repo root, but it
# also swallows this module's data/sql/db-world/**.sql, which is the ENTIRE module.
#
# The failure is delayed and quiet. `docker build` sends the whole working tree as context, so a
# LOCAL build picks the SQL up and everything works -- while CI, which builds from a clean
# `git clone`, produces an image with no migration in it and a worldserver that boots fine and
# grants nothing. `git status` never mentions the missing file.
#
# A nested .gitignore's patterns take precedence over the parent's for paths beneath it, so
# re-including the directory is enough. Re-including only *.sql would NOT be: git never descends
# into an excluded directory.
#
# The tidier fix is to anchor the root pattern as `/data/`. Do that instead and delete this file.
!/data/
